{
    "background_story": "Averie was a free-spirited artist who spent most of her days exploring the countryside in her rusty old van, affectionately named Willard. The two were inseparable, with Willard carrying Averie to hidden coves, secret waterfalls, and rolling hills that inspired her vibrant paintings. As she traveled, Averie collected stories and characters, weaving them into her art. Her studio, a cozy cabin on the outskirts of town, was filled with canvases depicting the beauty of the natural world. Locals would often remark on the uncanny resemblance between Averie's landscapes and the actual scenery, crediting Willard for taking her to the most breathtaking spots. Averie's art career flourished, but she never forgot the trusty companion that had been with her every step of the way \u2013 Willard, the faithful van that had become an extension of herself.",
